{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/docset at 7d540d2721eaad32301b77eccb1f351683892fac: the no-workroom citation-gate skip test made immune to an inherited Git environment.\n\nWHAT WAS WRONG, restated from the review that found it. The gate has two skips — no workroom in this checkout, and a genesis mismatch — and the test asserted only that some skip occurred. The subprocess inherited the caller's environment, and app.Open resolves through git, which honours GIT_DIR over the walk-up. With GIT_DIR set the subprocess reached a real workroom, skipped for the genesis mismatch, and the test passed while proving the wrong branch.\n\nTHE REPAIR. The subprocess environment now drops GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE and GIT_COMMON_DIR, so the checkout under test is the temporary directory by construction rather than by luck; and the assertion requires the no-workroom reason rather than the skip prefix.\n\nPROVED, NOT ASSUMED. This is the fix my own review recommended, which is a reason for more scepticism rather than less, so I ran the case that produced the finding rather than accepting a green suite.\n\n- Clean environment: passes.\n- Hostile GIT_DIR: passes, and a probe printing the subprocess output confirms it now takes anchor_test.go:43, \"no workroom in this checkout\" — the intended branch. I record this because passing under a hostile environment is the correct outcome here and would otherwise look like the original bug; what changed is which branch it proves.\n- Environment stripping removed, GIT_DIR set: FAILS on the reason assertion, \"citation gate did not skip for the absent workroom\". So the reason check has teeth against exactly the skip that used to satisfy the old test.\n- Both changes removed, GIT_DIR set: passes wrongly. The original defect reproduces, which is what shows the two halves together are what fix it.\n\nI also corrected my own promise while doing this. I had written that the hostile case must now fail. That was wrong: stripping the variables makes the test environment-independent, so it should pass, and the proof is which reason it observes, not the exit status.\n\nSCOPE. New-file-only, as required: the diff against the reviewed head touches internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go alone. Existing gate behaviour is unchanged. internal/docset/citation_test.go is unformatted on the base commit and remains so; I did not touch it and did not reformat it, since that would widen the diff beyond the new file.\n\nGATES at this exact head: make docs 0, make test 0 across twenty packages with no failures, git diff --check clean.\n\nONE DEVIATION, stated so it is not a surprise at merge. The request named the existing request/docset-no-workroom-skip branch. That branch is checked out in another worktree at the reviewed head and is not on origin, so committing to it would have meant writing into another actor's working directory. I built the repair from that exact commit on repair/docset-no-workroom-skip, pushed to origin, and the head is a direct child of a2e3f187.","body":{"commit":"7d540d2721eaad32301b77eccb1f351683892fac","path":"internal/docset"}}